+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## DOM Stability Defect
+
+**Problem:** The acceptance suite (Cypress in a real browser) fails with "element has detached from DOM" errors when toggling todo completion state. The in-harness tests (happy-dom) do not catch this because happy-dom handles DOM operations differently.
+
+**Root cause:** `js/app.js` `render()` function clears `todoList.innerHTML = ''` and rebuilds all list elements from scratch on every state change. In a real browser, this invalidates element references that Cypress holds.
+
+**Fix required:** Preserve DOM element identity — mutate existing `<li>` nodes in place (toggle class, update checkbox) instead of re-rendering the entire list.
+
+**Spec added:** `features/dom-stability.feature` with 5 scenarios that fail on current code, requiring DOM nodes to remain attached after:
+1. Toggling a single todo's completed state (2 scenarios)
+2. Using toggle-all (2 scenarios)
+3. Navigating filter routes and back (1 scenario)
+
+**Step definitions added:** `features/support/steps.js` — "the user remembers the first todo-list li element" and "the remembered li element is still in the document"
+
+**Watchbill:** `watchbill.json` created with 5 target scenarios for QM to verify.
