+Feature: DOM element identity stability
+  As a user interacting with the todo list
+  I want DOM elements to remain stable across state changes
+  So that my browser's view of the list does not break mid-interaction
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Toggling a single todo preserves element identity
+
+    Scenario: Clicking a todo's checkbox keeps the existing DOM node attached
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | false     |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user remembers the first todo-list li element
+      And the user toggles the checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the remembered li element is still in the document
+
+    Scenario: Unchecking a completed todo keeps the existing DOM node attached
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | true      |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user remembers the first todo-list li element
+      And the user toggles the checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the remembered li element is still in the document
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all preserves element identity
+
+    Scenario: Clicking toggle-all keeps existing DOM nodes attached
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | false     |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user remembers the first todo-list li element
+      And the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then the remembered li element is still in the document
+
+    Scenario: Unchecking toggle-all keeps existing DOM nodes attached
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | true      |
+        | Walk the dog | true      |
+      When the user remembers the first todo-list li element
+      And the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then the remembered li element is still in the document
+
+  Rule: Routing preserves element identity
+
+    Scenario: Navigating to a filter and back does not destroy existing elements
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | true      |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user remembers the first todo-list li element
+      And the user navigates to "#/active"
+      And the user navigates to "#/"
+      Then the remembered li element is still in the document
